 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "sentences is a non-empty list of sentences, each a sequence of words separated by single spaces, and maxWidth is a positive integer at least as long as every word. Level 3 (inferred extension): wrap each sentence greedily into lines of at most maxWidth as in level 2, then justify fully as in LeetCode 68: every line except the last line of its sentence and except single-word lines gets extra spaces between words so its length is exactly maxWidth, spread as evenly as possible with leftmost gaps receiving one more; last and single-word lines stay left-aligned. The inner width is maxWidth. Each box is a top border \"+\" followed by inner-width \"-\" characters and \"+\", then one content line per box line made of \"|\", the line padded on the right with spaces to the inner width, and \"|\", then a bottom border equal to the top. Boxes are listed one after another, each with its own borders. Return the list of output lines.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
